W: 1. 'Twas on one April morning, just as the sun was rising,
W: 'Twas on one April morning, I heard the small birds sing.
W: They were singing Lovely Nancy,
W: For love it is a fancy,
W: And sweet were the notes that I heard the small birds sing.
W:
W: 2. Young men are false and are full of all deceiving;
W: Young men are false, and they seldom do prove true.
W: For they're roving and they're ranging
W: And their minds are always changing
W: And they're thinking for to find out some other girl that's new.
W:
W: 3. O if I had but my own heart in keeping,
W: O if I had but my own heart back again:
W: Close in my bosom
W: I would lock it up forever
W: And it should wander never so far from me again.
W:
W: 4. So why would you spend all your long time in courting?
W: Why would you spend all your long time in vain?
W: For I don't intend to marry,
W: I would rather longer tarry.
W: O young man, don't you spend all your single life in vain.
W:
W: (Repeat first verse)
